From: Ethan Zou <gloridust@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 01:45:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/mdp5: don't flush or wait for PP_DONE on a
 switched-off CRTC

With the screen blanked through fbdev the CRTC stays enabled but
inactive, and fbcon (or anything drawing into the fbdev buffer) keeps
committing plane updates to it. mdp5_crtc_atomic_flush() then programs
the runtime-suspended MDP and, for a command-mode panel, re-arms the
PP_DONE completion, which can never fire because the interface is off.
Every such commit then stalls twice for the 50 ms timeout and logs

  msm_mdp 901000.display-controller: pp done time out, lm=2

several times a second for as long as the screen is off (Xiaomi Mi 5,
JDI R63452 command-mode panel).

Skip the hardware flush for an inactive CRTC (sending its event right
away), don't wait for a flush that never happened, and complete the
PP_DONE completion when the CRTC is disabled so nothing is left waiting
on it.
---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/mdp5/mdp5_crtc.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/mdp5/mdp5_crtc.c
@@ -501,8 +501,11 @@ static void mdp5_crtc_atomic_disable(struct drm_crtc *crtc,
 	/* Disable/save vblank irq handling before power is disabled */
 	drm_crtc_vblank_off(crtc);
 
-	if (mdp5_cstate->cmd_mode)
+	if (mdp5_cstate->cmd_mode) {
 		mdp_irq_unregister(&mdp5_kms->base, &mdp5_crtc->pp_done);
+		/* no PP_DONE will come any more: don't leave waiters hanging */
+		complete_all(&mdp5_crtc->pp_completion);
+	}
 
 	mdp_irq_unregister(&mdp5_kms->base, &mdp5_crtc->err);
 	pm_runtime_put_sync(dev);
@@ -818,6 +821,21 @@ static void mdp5_crtc_atomic_flush(struct drm_crtc *crtc,
 	if (unlikely(!mdp5_cstate->ctl))
 		return;
 
+	/*
+	 * Plane updates on a CRTC that is switched off (e.g. fbcon drawing
+	 * while the screen is blanked): the MDP is runtime-suspended, so don't
+	 * touch it, and a command-mode panel would never signal PP_DONE.
+	 */
+	if (!crtc->state->active) {
+		spin_lock_irqsave(&dev->event_lock, flags);
+		if (mdp5_crtc->event) {
+			drm_crtc_send_vblank_event(crtc, mdp5_crtc->event);
+			mdp5_crtc->event = NULL;
+		}
+		spin_unlock_irqrestore(&dev->event_lock, flags);
+		return;
+	}
+
 	blend_setup(crtc);
 
 	/* PP_DONE irq is only used by command mode for now.
@@ -1310,6 +1328,10 @@ void mdp5_crtc_wait_for_commit_done(struct drm_crtc *crtc)
 {
 	struct mdp5_crtc_state *mdp5_cstate = to_mdp5_crtc_state(crtc->state);
 
+	/* nothing was flushed to a switched-off CRTC (see atomic_flush) */
+	if (!crtc->state->active)
+		return;
+
 	if (mdp5_cstate->cmd_mode)
 		mdp5_crtc_wait_for_pp_done(crtc);
 	else
